11
00:58:20,869 --> 00:58:26,869
Sicario is a 2015 American action crime thriller film directed by Denis Villeneuve, written by Taylor
Sheridan in his screenwriting debut and starring Emily Blunt, Benicio del Toro, and Josh Brolin.

12
01:03:39,130 --> 01:03:45,130
The film follows a principled FBI special agent who is enlisted by a government task
force to bring down the leader of a powerful and brutal Mexican drug cartel.

13
01:08:57,391 --> 01:09:03,391
Sicario was selected to compete for the Palme d'Or
at the 2015 Cannes Film Festival.

14
01:14:15,652 --> 01:14:21,652
It began a limited release in the United States on September 18, 2015,
followed by a nationwide release on October 2, 2015.

15
01:19:33,913 --> 01:19:39,913
Sicario received praise for its cast performances, writing,
direction, musical score and cinematography.

16
01:24:52,173 --> 01:24:58,173
The film was nominated for Best Cinematography, Best Original Score,
and Best Sound Editing at the 88th Academy Awards.

17
01:30:10,434 --> 01:30:16,434
It also earned BAFTA nominations for Best Supporting Actor,
Best Cinematography, and Best Film Music.

18
01:35:28,695 --> 01:35:34,695
Its sequel, Sicario: Day of the Soldado, directed by
Stefano Sollima, was released on June 29, 2018.

19
01:40:46,956 --> 01:40:52,956
A third film, titled Sicario: Capos, is in development.

20
01:46:05,217 --> 01:46:11,217
The film is the first installment of writer Taylor Sheridan's American
Frontier Trilogy, proceeding Hell or High Water and Wind River.

21
01:51:23,478 --> 01:51:29,478
The film explores themes of mission, assassin, central
intelligence agency (cia), mexico, corruption.

22
01:56:41,739 --> 01:56:47,739
The tone is dark and intense.
